hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19681","Hushaym narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim al-Ansari informed us from Kharijah ibn Zayd from his uncle Yazid ibn Thabit, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we reached al-Baqi, there was a new grave. He asked about it, and it was said: So-and-so woman, and he recognized her. He said: Did you not inform me of her. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you were resting and fasting, and we disliked to inform you. He said: Do not do so, no dead among you shall die while I am among you but inform me of him, for my prayer over him is a mercy for him. He said: Then he came to the grave and arranged us behind him and said four takbirs over it."
"19682","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from Uthman, meaning Ibn Hakim, from Kharijah ibn Zayd from his uncle Yazid ibn Thabit, that he was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his companions, when a funeral appeared. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, he rose and his companions rose with him, and they remained standing until it passed. He said: By Allah, I do not know whether from annoyance at it or from narrowness of the place, and I do not think it but a Jew or a Jewess. And we did not ask about his standing (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
